# REITs (Real Estate Investment Trusts)

REITs are companies that own or finance income-producing real estate. They trade like stocks on public exchanges and are required to distribute at least 90% of taxable income as dividends.

## Types

- **Equity REITs**: Own properties (office, retail, residential)
- **Mortgage REITs**: Finance mortgages (riskier)
- **Hybrid REITs**: Both ownership and financing

## Key Characteristics

- Liquid (trade daily like stocks)
- Diversified across many properties
- Regular dividends
- Professional management
- Interest rate sensitivity
- Leverage on balance sheet

## Major REIT ETFs

- [[VNQ]] (Vanguard Real Estate ETF)
- [[SCHH]] (Schwab U.S. REIT ETF)
- [[RWO]] (iShares S&P Developed Intl. Property ETF)

